nodecode-checkin is a rewrite of capthvnsen's capthvnsen/alans-way-agents:

  https://github.com/capthvnsen/alans-way-agents
  commit 0f65549ac1353f6b74b8ac6a22d58f3eb6dea0a3
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Alan's Way contributors (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's proactivity engine and its one tool. The
idle rule is the original's -- a base wait that doubles for each check-in
left unanswered, capped at a week, firing only inside the operator's waking
hours and moved to the next active hour when the wait runs out overnight --
with the same morning brief at the head of the day, the same state it keeps
(the last exchange, the last check-in, the unanswered count, the last brief),
the same three moves a due check-in offers the model, the same "[SILENT] when
nothing is worth their attention", the same safety line, and a state file a
restart resumes from. The tool is the original's too, quieter-only: a change
that would make check-ins reach further is refused with the exact command to
tell the operator to send. The operator's own command carries the same
verbs, and its reading of the clock is the same, with one deliberate
difference: a cell cannot ask a host for a named IANA zone, so the section
carries the operator's UTC offset in minutes instead of a zone name.

What was left out, and why: the texting voice rides each chat turn as a
context note (the original's note, shortened) and a `/checkin voice` switch
turns it off; the original's per-reply polish -- stripping a leading
"Certainly!" at send time -- is not carried over, because a Nodecode cell sees
the answer before it is posted through no one seam the rewrite could take
without owning the channel. The four workspace skills are prose for a
separate companion desktop app and its browser bridge, which the rewrite does
not bundle. Cross-bot proactivity, the second bot's shared digest directory
and its cross_bot_ask tool, and the profile and CLI surfaces of a Python host
are not carried over: a Nodecode home is one organism, and the cell binds the
one session the operator names. The check-in's own delivery is the session's:
the cell puts a prompt in and the answer reaches wherever that session's chats
go.
